 Shows pop-up dictionary that searches the selected word on the page.
 
+#### `contents.getNativeTextInputState()`
+
+Returns `Object` - An experimental, observation-only snapshot of Chromium's
+cached native editing state. This OpenCraft fork method is not an input
+authorization token or an atomic renderer snapshot.
+
+* `observationOnly` boolean - Always true.
+* `coordinateSpace` string - Always `root-viewport-dip`.
+* `active` boolean - Whether a native text input target is active.
+* `nodeId` Integer (optional) - Document-local node identity, not globally unique.
+* `type` Integer (optional) - Native text input type.
+* `mode` Integer (optional) - Native text input mode.
+* `password` boolean (optional) - Whether the native target is a password field.
+* `selection` Object (optional) - UTF-16 offsets in the native editing context.
+  * `start` number
+  * `end` number
+* `composition` Object (optional) - Current native composition's UTF-16 offsets.
+  * `start` number
+  * `end` number
+* `caretBounds` Rectangle (optional) - Native selection focus edge or EditContext
+  selection bounds, in root viewport DIPs. An insertion edge may have zero width.
+
+No field text is returned. Missing `caretBounds` means geometry is unavailable;
+callers must not substitute guessed character or control bounds. State and
+geometry arrive through separate Chromium updates and may be temporarily stale.
+
 #### `contents.isOffscreen()`
 
 Returns `boolean` - Indicates whether _offscreen rendering_ is enabled.
